§ `The limb for a company, a limited liability company or a bank applies only to a person of that kind`

-- "in the case of a company": an individual is not a company.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8: the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `text V1` `event: creditors winding up` `an individual` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8: the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `text V2f` `event: creditors winding up` `a bank` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8: the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `text V2f` `event: administration order` `an individual` FALSE
-- "in the case of a limited liability company".
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8: the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `text V2c` `event: llc winding up` `a company` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8: the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `text V2f` `event: llc winding up` `an individual` FALSE
-- "in the case of a bank".
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8: the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `text V2b` `event: bank winding up` `a company` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8: the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `text V2f` `event: bank winding up` `an individual` FALSE
-- The Law does not say whether a bank or a limited liability company is also a "company": a person the caller says is both is reached by either limb.
#ASSERT `Article 8: the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `text V2f` `event: creditors winding up` (`a person of the kind` TRUE TRUE FALSE) FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 8: the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `text V2f` `event: llc winding up` (`a person of the kind` TRUE TRUE FALSE) FALSE
-- Limbs (a) to (d) say "that person": no kind is needed.
#ASSERT `Article 8: the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `text V1` `event: own application` `an individual` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 8: the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `text V2f` `event: own application` `a bank` FALSE

§ `The paragraph of the text that lists the event`

-- The bank limb is (f) in V2b and (g) from V2c: the same event, a different letter, because the limited liability company limb was inserted before it.
#ASSERT `Article 8: the paragraph of the text that lists the event` `text V2b` `event: bank winding up` EQUALS "(f)"
#ASSERT `Article 8: the paragraph of the text that lists the event` `text V2c` `event: bank winding up` EQUALS "(g)"
#ASSERT `Article 8: the paragraph of the text that lists the event` `text V2d` `event: bank winding up` EQUALS "(g)"
#ASSERT `Article 8: the paragraph of the text that lists the event` `text V2e` `event: bank winding up` EQUALS "(g)"
#ASSERT `Article 8: the paragraph of the text that lists the event` `text V2f` `event: bank winding up` EQUALS "(g)"
#ASSERT `Article 8: the paragraph of the text that lists the event` `text V2c` `event: llc winding up` EQUALS "(f)"
#ASSERT `Article 8: the paragraph of the text that lists the event` `text V2f` `event: llc winding up` EQUALS "(f)"
#ASSERT `Article 8: the paragraph of the text that lists the event` `text V2f` `event: administration order` EQUALS "(ea)"
#ASSERT `Article 8: the paragraph of the text that lists the event` `text V1` `event: own application` EQUALS "(a)"
#ASSERT `Article 8: the paragraph of the text that lists the event` `text V2a` `event: en desastre` EQUALS "(b)"
#ASSERT `Article 8: the paragraph of the text that lists the event` `text V2b` `event: debt remission` EQUALS "(ba)"
#ASSERT `Article 8: the paragraph of the text that lists the event` `text V2c` `event: general cession` EQUALS "(c)"
#ASSERT `Article 8: the paragraph of the text that lists the event` `text V2d` `event: renounced` EQUALS "(d)"
#ASSERT `Article 8: the paragraph of the text that lists the event` `text V2e` `event: creditors winding up` EQUALS "(e)"
-- No paragraph, where the text does not list the event.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 8: the paragraph of the text that lists the event` `text V2e` `event: administration order`
        BECAUSE "no paragraph of this text of Article 8 lists the event"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 8: the paragraph of the text that lists the event` `text V1` `event: bank winding up`
        BECAUSE "no paragraph of this text of Article 8 lists the event"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 8: the paragraph of the text that lists the event` `text V2f` `event: some other event`
        BECAUSE "no paragraph of this text of Article 8 lists the event"

§ `A contrary intention appears, and the years before 2019`

#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 8: the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `text V1` `event: own application` `an individual` TRUE
        BECAUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 8 does not say what a reference to a person becoming bankrupt then means"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 8: the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `text V2f` `event: bank winding up` `a bank` TRUE
        BECAUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 8 does not say what a reference to a person becoming bankrupt then means"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 8: the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `text inferred` `event: own application` `an individual` FALSE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 8: the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `text none` `event: own application` `an individual` FALSE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 8: the paragraph of the text that lists the event` `text inferred` `event: own application`
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"

§ `Fork I2: the day that selects the text of Article 8`

-- An administration order made on 15 January 2026, asked about on 28 October 2026.  Limb (ea) came into force on 19 June 2026.
-- Taken (the day of the event): the text of 15 January 2026 is V2e, which has no such limb.  The other reading (the day on which the question about the event is asked): V2f.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8: on the day of the event and the day of the question, the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `event: administration order` `a company` (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day of the event`
#ASSERT `Article 8: on the day of the event and the day of the question, the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `event: administration order` `a company` (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day on which the question about the event is asked`
-- The edge: 18 June 2026 is the last day of V2e; 19 June 2026 is the first day of V2f.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8: on the day of the event and the day of the question, the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `event: administration order` `a company` (YMD 2026 6 18) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day of the event`
#ASSERT `Article 8: on the day of the event and the day of the question, the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `event: administration order` `a company` (YMD 2026 6 19) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day of the event`
-- Asked about on the day of the event itself, the two readings agree.
#ASSERT `Article 8: on the day of the event and the day of the question, the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `event: administration order` `a company` (YMD 2026 6 19) (YMD 2026 6 19) FALSE `the day on which the question about the event is asked`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8: on the day of the event and the day of the question, the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `event: administration order` `a company` (YMD 2026 6 18) (YMD 2026 6 18) FALSE `the day on which the question about the event is asked`
-- The bank limb: the day before and the day of its insertion (31 January 2022).
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8: on the day of the event and the day of the question, the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `event: bank winding up` `a bank` (YMD 2022 1 30) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day of the event`
#ASSERT `Article 8: on the day of the event and the day of the question, the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `event: bank winding up` `a bank` (YMD 2022 1 31) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day of the event`
#ASSERT `Article 8: on the day of the event and the day of the question, the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `event: bank winding up` `a bank` (YMD 2022 1 30) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day on which the question about the event is asked`
-- The limited liability company limb: the day before and the day of its insertion (1 September 2022).
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8: on the day of the event and the day of the question, the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `event: llc winding up` `a limited liability company` (YMD 2022 8 31) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day of the event`
#ASSERT `Article 8: on the day of the event and the day of the question, the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `event: llc winding up` `a limited liability company` (YMD 2022 9 1) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day of the event`
-- 28 September 2021 (the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021) changes Article 1 but not Article 8: a limb present in both V1 and V2a gives the same answer on both sides of the day.
#ASSERT `Article 8: on the day of the event and the day of the question, the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `event: own application` `an individual` (YMD 2021 9 27) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day of the event`
#ASSERT `Article 8: on the day of the event and the day of the question, the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `event: own application` `an individual` (YMD 2021 9 28) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day of the event`
-- An event before 1 January 2019: no text is deposited for the day of the event, so the day-of-the-event reading refuses; the day-the-question-is-asked reading answers from the text of that day.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 8: on the day of the event and the day of the question, the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `event: own application` `an individual` (YMD 2018 12 31) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day of the event`
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"
#ASSERT `Article 8: on the day of the event and the day of the question, the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `event: own application` `an individual` (YMD 2018 12 31) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day on which the question about the event is asked`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 8: on the day of the event and the day of the question, the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `event: own application` `an individual` (YMD 2010 6 15) (YMD 2018 6 15) FALSE `the day on which the question about the event is asked`
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"
-- A contrary intention refuses on either reading.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 8: on the day of the event and the day of the question, the event is a person becoming bankrupt` `event: own application` `an individual` (YMD 2024 5 1) (YMD 2026 10 28) TRUE `the day of the event`
        BECAUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 8 does not say what a reference to a person becoming bankrupt then means"

